# Before, a failed earlier input `have k N = -1` left k occupied in
# ParseScope even though exec_stmt discarded its temporary ExecEnv.
# The active correction below then failed with "already bound".
#
# Current: the run transaction restores parse scopes on failure, so the
# correction succeeds in the same Runtime. The executable failed-input
# boundary is tested in tests/unit/run/binding_lifecycle/tests.rs.
# Gate: target/release/litex -strict -f examples/stmt_nodes/definition/parse_scope_transaction.lit

have k N = 1
k = 1
